Z||000001||Wolfhound||03-27-2001||05:31 AM||||I have one and will check at first light. I think it might be a single wire by the drivers side henge. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-27-2001||11:10 AM||||I believe on 84's it is as wolfhound described.<P>On my 87, it is found in the 4 cavity weather pack connector on the right side hinge.  There are 4 wires on the firewall side, and if your car did not come with the power trunk release from the factory, there will only be 3 wires on the decklid side.  All the wires inside the car are there.<P>good info also found at the ogre's cave.  check out the link at the bottom of any Forum page.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-27-2001||12:10 PM||||It comes out like Wolfhound said a single wire by the drivers side hinge. Most of the time when one is not working it is a bad ground.<P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
